  "live_records": {
    "q-81876": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81876",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242839/assets/6688df8ff828aa97aa091fe7c3cff421aab184fde71092e64377718522686fa1.png)\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube?",
      "worked_solution": "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=10\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(10\\,\\text{m})^{3}=1\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$",
