    "q-107177": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107177",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the cube whose sides each have length $4\\,\\text{in}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=4\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(4\\,\\text{in})^{3}=64\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$",
