    "q-107268": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107268",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242839/assets/df0c2e8a1af51ce0765ca2689f2ee1043d940d2abe2f8f18616786ace1fb18ac.png)\n\nThe volume of the cube above is $1\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.$ What is the length of its sides?",
      "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{1}=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $1\\,\\text{m}.$",
